@* DS parity — no consumer yet: the recipe dialog's Ingredients and Method adopt it in the design-system rollout. *@
@*
    OdsSortableList — an editable, reorderable list of rows (Odyssey Design System · components/SortableList,
    version 1795477868-c9a2): the recipe dialog's Ingredients and Method are the first two. Each row is a
    compact card — handle · the consumer's RenderItem cells · ⋯ — moved three ways that all end in OnMove:

      • drag — press the handle (drag_indicator) and drag. The row dims with a dashed outline and a 3px
        primary line in the gap shows where it lands; nothing shifts. The nearest scrolling ancestor scrolls
        near its edge. Pointer events (mouse, pen, touch) — the geometry is wwwroot/js/sortable-list.js;
      • keys — on the focused handle Space / Enter lifts (aria-pressed), ↑ / ↓ move one place, Space / Enter
        drops, Escape puts it back where it started and does NOT close an enclosing dialog (the JS module
        stops that key before MudDialog's interceptor sees it), Tab drops. Each step is announced in the
        list's own assertive live region;
      • menu — the row's ⋯ (OdsMenu): Move up · Move down · — · Remove, the single-pointer alternative
        WCAG 2.5.7 asks of a drag. A move the row cannot make is absent (the menu's rule).

    Wherever a row lands it flashes a primary ring once (none under reduced motion). Each row is a
    <fieldset data-sort-row> with an sr-only legend from GetLabel ("Ingredient 3"). A heading row
    (IsHeading) is a tinted band, flush left; once the list has one, every other row and the Header step in
    one gutter. Moving a heading moves only the heading. Styled by .odc-sortable / .odc-sort-*.
*@
@typeparam TItem
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime Js

<div @ref="_list" class="@RootClass">
    <span class="odc-sr-only" id="@HelpId">@DragHint</span>
    <div class="odc-sr-only" role="status" aria-live="assertive">@_say</div>
    @if (Header is not null)
    {
        <div class="@($"odc-sortable-head {HeaderClass}".TrimEnd())" aria-hidden="true">@Header</div>
    }
    @for (var i = 0; i < Items.Count; i++)
    {
        var index = i;
        var item = Items[i];
        var key = KeyOf(item);
        var label = LabelOf(item, index);
        var keysLifted = _drag is { Mode: DragMode.Keys } d && Equals(d.Key, key);
        <fieldset @key="key" class="@RowClassFor(item, index, key)" data-sort-row>
            <legend class="odc-sr-only">@Cap(label)</legend>
            <button type="button" id="@HandleId(key)" class="@(keysLifted ? "odc-sort-handle on" : "odc-sort-handle")"
                    data-sort-handle="@index"
                    aria-label="@($"Move {label}")" aria-describedby="@HelpId"
                    aria-pressed="@(keysLifted ? "true" : "false")"
                    @onkeydown="e => OnHandleKeyDownAsync(e, index)">
                <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">drag_indicator</span>
            </button>
            @if (RenderItem is not null)
            {
                @RenderItem(new OdsSortableItem<TItem>(item, index))
            }
            <div class="odc-sort-menu">
                <OdsMenu Items="MenuFor(item, index, label)" AriaLabel="@($"Actions for {label}")" />
            </div>
        </fieldset>
    }
</div>
